summary:
  Turning timeshift off in the settings sends a parked station back to
  live, which raises the standing order and starts the stream.

history:
  Found 2026-09-21 reading issue #13 against the code: tsPlayLive was called
  for a parked station and for one paused inside its buffer, so a checkbox
  in the settings put the radio back on over the listener's pause.

target:
  package/contents/ui/main.qml

find:
              if (root._tsPaused || (timeshift.shifted && !isPlaying())) stopWithFade();
              else if (timeshift.shifted) tsPlayLive(timeshift.streamUrl);

replace:
              if (false) stopWithFade();
              else if (timeshift.shifted || root._tsPaused) tsPlayLive(timeshift.streamUrl);

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_invariants.py::test_unticking_timeshift_does_not_wake_a_listener_who_said_quiet.
  Line-neutral.
